K60 MFB candidate patch: unimplemented IOMFB selectors answer success.

Merge of the reference 0046 semantics with the K60 MiniIOMobileFramebuffer
design intent, as agreed for Alternative D (candidate only: NOT added to
patches/xnu/series, kernel NOT rebuilt).

Semantics:
- default path (selector has no case): keep the once-per-selector log, zero
  every requested scalar output and the structure output (when no output
  descriptor is attached), and return kIOReturnSuccess. This mirrors sweet
  0046-sweet-iosurface-iomfb.patch: externalMethod seeds
  IOReturn ret = kIOReturnSuccess (line 1370) and its default: break falls
  through to return ret with zeroed outputs (lines 1425-1447).
- exception kept from the K60 design intent (the old comment at
  MiniIOMobileFramebuffer.cpp:1390-1392): GetGammaTable must not succeed with
  an all-zero LUT -- that describes a black display. Selector 27 =
  _kern_GetGammaTable[StructMethod] per the 20G81 IOMobileFramebuffer
  framework kern_* table (sweet NOTES.md:114); a 20G81 backboardd was
  observed calling IOMFB selectors 57, 15, 22, 29, 33, 79, 74, 12, 6, 27,
  17, 84, 50 and surviving the 0046 all-success backend (sweet NOTES.md:86),
  so 27 is the only query this backend refuses.
- SetGammaTable (selector 17, same table) stays on the success path: this
  software backend never consumes the table, so a written-but-ignored table
  cannot blacken the panel.
- explicit unsupported cases above the default are untouched: GetDisplayArea
  (falls back to the framework default), GetBlock outside block 0x40, and
  GetDotPitch without a DPI value.

Basis:
- refs/ios-sweet-k60/xnu/patches/0046-sweet-iosurface-iomfb.patch:1370
  (ret = kIOReturnSuccess) and :1425-1447 (default: break -> zeroed outputs,
  return ret).
- refs/ios-sweet-k60/NOTES.md:86 (boot 0052n: backboardd opens the display
  and walks selectors 57, 15, 22, 29, 33, 79, 74, 12, 6, 27, 17, 84, 50).
- refs/ios-sweet-k60/NOTES.md:114 (kern_* selector table: 27 GetGammaTable,
  17 SetGammaTable, 15 SetDebugFlags).
- iokit/Kernel/MiniIOMobileFramebuffer.cpp:1390-1392 (K60 design intent
  comment this patch partially preserves).

Verification: git apply --check on a clean copy of the effective
out/mondrian/ipados-16.6.1-20G81/mondrian/tree/.cache/xnu-work tree
(sideD-check.log). The series resolver (scripts/unixnu/patches.py:59) uses
git apply, so this quilt-style header is accepted.
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/MiniIOMobileFramebuffer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/MiniIOMobileFramebuffer.cpp
index 666b399..7aa5b65 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/MiniIOMobileFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/MiniIOMobileFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -55,6 +55,7 @@ enum {
 	kFBMethodSwapSignal             = 20,
 	kFBMethodSetDisplayDevice       = 22,
 	kFBMethodGetDigitalOutState     = 25,
+	kFBMethodGetGammaTable          = 27,
 	kFBMethodGetDotPitch            = 28,
 	kFBMethodGetDisplayArea         = 29,
 	kFBMethodSetColorRemapMode      = 33,
@@ -1387,10 +1388,35 @@ IOMobileFramebufferUserClient::externalMethod(uint32_t selector, IOExternalMetho
 		    args->scalarInputCount > 1 ? in[1] : 0, args->scalarInputCount > 2 ? in[2] : 0, args->scalarOutputCount,
 		    args->structureInputSize, args->structureOutputSize);
 	}
-	/* In particular, GetGammaTable must not succeed with an all-zero LUT:
-	 * that describes a black display. Unsupported hardware queries/setters
-	 * must leave the framework's software/default path in charge. */
-	return kIOReturnUnsupported;
+	/* Merged semantics: the reference 0046 backend seeds
+	 * IOReturn ret = kIOReturnSuccess and answers every unimplemented
+	 * selector with zeroed outputs and success; a 20G81 backboardd walked
+	 * IOMFB selectors 57, 15, 22, 29, 33, 79, 74, 12, 6, 27, 17, 84, 50 and
+	 * kept going (sweet NOTES.md:86). Keep that behaviour, but preserve the
+	 * K60 design intent for the one hardware query that must never be
+	 * faked: GetGammaTable (selector 27, _kern_GetGammaTable[StructMethod]
+	 * in the 20G81 framework's kern_* table, sweet NOTES.md:114) must not
+	 * succeed with an all-zero LUT -- that describes a black display.
+	 * Other query-type selectors keep their explicit unsupported cases
+	 * above (GetDisplayArea, GetBlock outside block 0x40, GetDotPitch
+	 * without a DPI value). SetGammaTable (selector 17) stays on the
+	 * success path: this software backend never consumes the table, so a
+	 * written-but-ignored table cannot blacken the panel. */
+	if (selector == kFBMethodGetGammaTable) {
+		return kIOReturnUnsupported;
+	}
+
+	/* Unimplemented selector: answer like the reference 0046 backend --
+	 * zero every requested output and report success. */
+	if (args->scalarOutput != NULL) {
+		for (uint32_t i = 0; i < args->scalarOutputCount; i++) {
+			args->scalarOutput[i] = 0;
+		}
+	}
+	if (args->structureOutputDescriptor == NULL && args->structureOutput != NULL) {
+		bzero(args->structureOutput, args->structureOutputSize);
+	}
+	return kIOReturnSuccess;
 }
 
